The function's behavior is unchanged. The rewrite copies the field array pointer and field count into locals so the loop doesn't reload them through `mesg` on every iteration. It also uses a plain `unsigned` loop counter instead of `FIT_UINT16`, which avoids repeated 16-bit truncation. Without benchmarking, I'd expect only a small speedup.

```cpp
const FIT_UINT16 Profile::GetFieldIndex(const FIT_UINT16 mesgNum, const FIT_UINT8 fieldNum)
{
    const MESG *mesg = GetMesg(mesgNum);

    if (mesg == NULL)
        return FIT_UINT16_INVALID;

    const FIELD *fields = mesg->fields;
    const unsigned n = (unsigned)mesg->numFields;

    for (unsigned i = 0; i < n; i++)
    {
        if (fields[i].num == fieldNum)
            return (FIT_UINT16)i;
    }

    return FIT_UINT16_INVALID;
}
```